<section class="section demo-section" id="object-demo"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="section-label">A small peek under the hood</div><h2 class="section-title">JavaScript Object Demo</h2></div><p class="section-intro">This portfolio uses a Student object to display my details. Try a button and watch the object update.</p></div><div class="demo-layout"><div class="demo-copy"><h3>One object, a few useful details.</h3><p>The same student details power the introduction, education summary, subjects, and this interactive demo. The controls below demonstrate updating, deleting, and restoring object properties.</p><div class="demo-hint" id="methodOutput" aria-live="polite">Use “Show Name &amp; Section” to call the class method.</div></div><div class="demo-card reveal"><div class="demo-card-head"><h3>Student object</h3><span id="demoStatusBadge">Live data</span></div><dl class="demo-fields" id="studentDetails"></dl><div class="demo-result" id="demoMessage" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="demo-actions"><button class="primary" id="updateStatus">Update Status</button><button id="deleteEmail">Delete Email</button><button id="restoreStudent">Restore Student</button><button id="showNameSection">Show Name &amp; Section</button></div></div></div></div></section>
